.TH SDL_SetAtomicPointer 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SetAtomicPointer \- Set a pointer to a value atomically.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_atomic.h>
.PP
.BI "void * SDL_SetAtomicPointer(void **a, void *v);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR "Note: If you don\(aqt know what this function is for, you shouldn\(aqt use it!"

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I a
a pointer to a pointer\[char46]
.TP
.I v
the desired pointer value\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the previous value of the pointer\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

